'''''Sagina nodosa''''', the '''knotted pearlwort''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |access-date=2014-10-17}}</ref> is a species in the genus ''[[Sagina]]'', native to northern [[Europe]]. It is a low-growing plant up to 15&nbsp;cm tall, with paired [[leaf|leaves]] up to 1&nbsp;cm long. The [[flower]]s are 5–10&nbsp;mm diameter, with five white petals.<ref name=blamey>Blamey, M. & Grey-Wilson, C. (1989). ''Flora of Britain and Northern Europe''. {{ISBN|0-340-40170-2}}</ref><ref name=fnwe>Flora of NW Europe: [http://ip30.eti.uva.nl/BIS/flora.php?selected=beschrijving&menuentry=soorten&id=1926 ''Sagina nodosa'']{{dead link|date=May 2018 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

